        "content": "Web search results for query: \"\"Cursor 3\" agent-first workspace reactions community feedback\"\n\nI'll perform a web search for information about Cursor 3, its agent-first workspace, reactions, and community feedback.**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"Cursor 3 agent-first workspace reactions community feedback\",\"content_size\":\"high\"}\n```\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"Cursor 3 Changes Everything for Agentic Coding - YouTube\", \"link\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HTKGyLar8AU&vl=en\", \"content\": \"... Cursor 3 is here and it's a complete rebuild - new agent-first interface, Composer 2 model, embedded browser, parallel local + cloud agents .....\n                                                Based on my search, here's what I found about Cursor 3, its agent-first workspace, and community feedback:\n\n## Overview of Cursor 3\n\n**Cursor 3** (code-named \"Glass\") represents a complete rebuild of the Cursor interface, released around April 2, 2026. It's described not merely as an IDE upgrade, but as an **\"agent-first workspace\"** that fundamentally rethinks how developers interact with AI coding assistants.\n\n### Key Features:\n- **Agent-First Interface**: A new interface centered around agents rather than the traditional code editor\n- **Agents Window**: Multi-workspace interface allowing users and agents to work across different projects\n- **Parallel Agents**: Capability to run multiple local + cloud agents simultaneously\n- **Composer 2 Model**: New underlying AI model\n- **Embedded Browser**: Built-in browser functionality\n- **Design Mode**: Enhanced features for frontend work\n- **Worktrees**: Support for multiple working directories\n\n## Community Reactions\n\nThe feedback has been **sharply divided**:\n\n### Positive Reactions:\n- Developers praised it for scenarios requiring **multiple parallel tasks** that benefit from agent delegation\n- Strong for **frontend work** and design-heavy projects\n- Agent usage in Cursor reportedly grew **15x in a single year**, suggesting strong adoption\n\n### Criticisms & Concerns:\n- Many questioned whether Cursor is **abandoning traditional IDE functionality**\n- Pushback from developers who prefer **code-first workflows** with precise, synchronous control\n- Some feel the product tries to do too much by combining \"ambient, background autonomy\" with \"precise, synchronous control\" in one interface\n- Concerns about whether the agent-first approach suits all development workflows\n\n### Notable Community Discussions:\n- Active discussions on **Reddit** and **Hacker News** with mixed opinions\n- One community member noted: *\"Agent-first needs ambient, background autonomy. Code-first needs precise, synchronous control. Trying to do both in one product means you're...\"* (implying the challenge of balancing both paradigms)\n\nThe consensus appears to be that Cursor 3 is **innovative but polarizing**—best suited for developers who want heavy AI agent integration, but potentially alienating for those who prefer traditional, code-centric development workflows.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
